    schema:datePosted "2026-08-21"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About Yepoda Clean K-Beauty Innovation. No compromises. Yepoda is a clean K-Beauty brand that actually proves it works. We make Korean skincare without any of the compromises. Everything is clinically tested, 100% vegan, and formulated above EU standards. So you get the innovation and the results that K-Beauty is known for, plus a real commitment to sustainability. And we make it genuinely fun and easy to use — skincare you actually look forward to. Founded in 2020 by Sander Joonyoung van Bladel and Veronika Strotmann, Yepoda is a certified B Corp™ and 1% for the Planet member, based in the heart of Berlin. Our products are available through our own online shop and, since March 2025, at Sephora Europe — online and in over 650 stores. With a team of 140+ brilliant individuals from around the world, we are actively shaping Yepoda's story every day. We are looking for an organized and detail-oriented Creative Operations Intern to support the Creative Operations Lead and help keep the creative team’s projects, systems, and information running smoothly. This is a great opportunity for someone at the beginning of their career who is interested in the intersection of project management, marketing, business operations, and creative work. You do not need to be an expert in our tools or processes — we are looking for someone who is curious, structured, eager to learn, and excited to grow their Creative Operations skill set over the course of the internship. Your Tasks Support the Creative Operations Lead with the day-to-day coordination and tracking of creative projects, deadlines, feedback, approvals, and deliverables. Help maintain the creative team’s Notion ticketing system and keep project information accurate and up to date. Review incoming tickets for missing information and support smooth handovers between stakeholders and the creative team. Assist with weekly planning, project status updates, meeting notes, action items, and stakeholder follow-ups. Collect and organize data for simple reporting on project volume, timelines, overdue work, and team capacity. Support project coordination and administrative tasks across campaigns, launches, and ongoing creative requests. Assist with the organization and migration of creative assets into a digital asset management system, including file auditing, naming, tagging, and quality checks. Help maintain process documentation, trackers, templates, and other Creative Operations resources. Your Profile You are at the beginning of your career, ideally with up to 1–2 years of relevant internship or professional experience. You are studying or have recently graduated in a field such as business, marketing, communications, project management, media, or a related area. You are organized, detail-oriented, and enjoy bringing structure to information and processes. You have an interest in how creative teams work, while also enjoying the coordination, planning, and operational side of projects. You communicate clearly, work collaboratively, and follow through reliably on tasks. You are comfortable working with spreadsheets, trackers, databases, or other structured information. You are curious, proactive, and keen to learn new tools and ways of working. Previous experience with tools such as Notion, Figma, Adobe Creative Cloud, Miro, or digital asset management systems is a plus, but not required. Some exposure to marketing, creative production, or project coordination through university, internships, working student roles, or previous employment is beneficial. You are fluent in English. What We Offer Dynamic Environment: The opportunity to work in a start-up environment surrounded by a passionate and dedicated team. Accelerate Your Career: Take on responsibility from day 1, with room for professional growth and advancement as the company continues to expand. Inspiring Workspace: Located in the heart of Berlin's Prenzlauer Berg, a dog-friendly office, with free drinks and snacks. Hybrid Working: We understand that sometimes you get more stuff done from home and need a change of scenery. We Value Diversity: We seek to build an inclusive workplace that welcomes people from all different backgrounds. A welcoming, international, dedicated team with flat hierarchies and trust by default. Employee Discounts: You’ll get to enjoy the Yepoda products at a discount and share it with friends and family to keep your glow going! Unique add-ons: Enjoy an Urban Sports membership package to help you stay active and healthy. Would you like to be part of the team? Then we'd love to hear from you! 🫰✨ Make sure to apply by clicking on the “Apply for this job” button below. Please upload your CV and Cover Letter in English language. Our Talent Acquisition team will review your application and get back to you as soon as possible. At Yepoda we are dedicated to providing equal employment opportunities to all individuals, regardless of race, color, ethnicity, ancestry, religion, national origin, citizenship, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, parental status, disability, or any other status protected by applicable law. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-yepoda ;
