<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-executive-assistant-moorgate-283217> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-22T01:26:57+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkatrade/executive-assistant-moorgate-283217> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "79a080c0853c324f0a34b2ffe469a57082c8abbeba28f1299d93c740f7b263e5" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-21T18:42:27+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-22T01:26:57+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "executive-assistant-moorgate-283217" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-21"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "As our next Executive Assistant to the CEO (Maternity Cover), you'll play a key role in helping us build the UK's go-to home improvement marketplace. You'll be the person our CEO relies on to keep the day-to-day running smoothly, owning their diary, priorities and the details that let them focus on the big calls. It's a 12-month fixed-term contract, based in our London (Moorgate) office, and a genuine seat close to the decisions shaping Checkatrade's next chapter. Forget long lists, here’s what you’ll actually spend your time on: Owning the CEO's diary end-to-end: prioritising what matters, protecting focus time, and making sure every meeting has a clear purpose and the right people in the room. Coordinating board and leadership meetings: pulling together papers, chasing actions, and making sure nothing falls through the cracks between sessions. Managing complex travel and itineraries, sorting the logistics so the CEO can turn up ready, without the faff. Acting as a trusted first point of contact for the CEO: handling sensitive and confidential information with discretion, and representing them well with senior stakeholders, investors and the exec team. Keeping the wider leadership team's rhythm on track: coordinating offsites, leadership meetings and cross-team moments that keep everyone aligned. Spotting where things could run better and just fixing them: you'll have real ownership over how the CEO's office operates day to day. It’s not about ticking every box. It’s about turning up curious, ready to crack on. You’ll do well here if you bring: Experience supporting a CEO, founder or senior executive in a fast-moving business, ideally at C-suite level. A sharp eye for detail and the judgement to know what's urgent, what's important, and what can wait. Total discretion with confidential and sensitive information: people trust you with the details that matter. A calm, organised approach under pressure, with the confidence to manage upwards and push back when needed. We believe great work deserves great rewards. Here’s just a taste: Competitive salary Cashplan (WPA) Holiday buy and sell Cycle to Work scheme Home and Tech scheme EV scheme (Octopus) Life insurance Pathway – Financial Wellbeing Payroll Giving Pension Planning TradePoint discount (B&Q) How we’ll get to know each other: Screening call with one of our Talent Acquisition Partners 1st stage interview with our Senior Executive Assistants 2nd Stage interview with the CEO If this sounds like the place where you can do your best work, we’d love to hear from you, even if you don’t tick every box Want to join our Talent Community and be one of the first to know about our vacancies? Register your interest on our Registration Form At the moment, this role isn’t open to visa sponsorship applications. About us We’re Checkatrade – the UK’s leading platform for finding a tradesperson. With more than 50,000 trades listed and over 6 million reviews, we help homeowners get jobs done right and help tradespeople grow their business. We’re growing fast, with big plans to become the go-to brand for home improvements. If you care about great work, take pride in the details, and want to make an impact, you’ll fit right in. Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-checkatrade ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-executive-assistant-moorgate-283217" ;
    schema:jobLocation [ a schema:Place ;
            schema:name "Moorgate London" ] ;
    schema:title "Executive Assistant" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkatrade/executive-assistant-moorgate-283217> .

<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-field-based-business-development-executive-newcastle-329418> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-22T01:26:57+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/deliveroo/field-based-business-development-executive-newcastle-329418> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "8fffdada291fd29a476e3787a7bbcef733c170288f1847cca1e23ae0557b20ca" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-21T14:39:42+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-22T01:26:57+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "field-based-business-development-executive-newcastle-329418" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-21"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Field-Based Business Development Executive - Newcastle Join us in our mission to transform the way people shop and eat, where impact, innovation, and growth drives everything we do. Our Commercial team sits at the centre of Deliveroo’s marketplace—shaping how we serve restaurants, grocers, and new verticals worldwide. From negotiating key partnerships to unlocking new revenue streams and crafting data-led growth strategies, we take on big challenges that move the business forward. If you thrive in fast-paced, commercial environments and want to influence the future of a global brand—this is the team for you. We’re looking for a Field Sales Executive to join our Newcastle team. This is a hybrid role. In this role, you’ll help us build relationships with new restaurant partners across the region, improving our proposition for customers and identifying ways to continue our fast growth. Get to know our Commercial team — what drives us, how we work, and what you can expect. What You’ll Be Doing You’ll be joining the Regional UK and Ireland team. The Regional UK and Ireland team drives Deliveroo's performance across all 4 nations of UKI. From Brighton, to Bognor to Belfast, we are experts in the local markets we serve, focusing on bringing the best possible selection to our customers and opportunities for growth to our partners. Here’s what your day-to-day might look like: Drive regional restaurant acquisition: Map, prospect, pitch, and close high-value restaurant partners across your region to expand our local market selection. Execute strategic business development: Engage with independent restaurants via physical visits, emails, calls, and social platforms to demonstrate the commercial value of Deliveroo’s technology. Own the commercial onboarding journey: Oversee the end-to-end partner onboarding process to ensure it is fast, efficient, and seamless for new partners. Structure high-impact partnerships: Negotiate contract terms and partnership structures that secure win-win commercial outcomes for both restaurants and Deliveroo. Act as a local territory expert: Develop deep insight into the regional food scene, mapping out up-and-coming culinary trends and identifying the key brands that local customers crave. What You’ll Need to Thrive Essential Proven new business acquisition: Demonstrated sales experience with a track record of actively targeting new business and consistently delivering against demanding commercial targets. Commercial negotiation skills: Strong commercial acumen with the ability to handle negotiations and structure profitable, sustainable deals. Autonomy and field-based resilience: A self-motivated, tenacious approach with the ability to work independently and spend significant time out on the road meeting prospects. Effective relationship building: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to connect with diverse business owners and present product value clearly. Mobility requirement: Possession of a valid UK driving licence and access to a vehicle to facilitate travel across the North East and Yorkshire region. Nice to Have Industry sector knowledge: Prior experience or a deep understanding of the economics of hospitality, food delivery, or high-growth marketplace operations. Why Join Us? At Deliveroo, you’ll do work that matters, solving real-world problems in a three-sided marketplace that’s constantly evolving. We’re food lovers, problem solvers, community builders and more, brought together by a shared drive to make things better. Working here you can expect to: 🔧 Make a visible impact every day Your work directly improves experiences for customers, partners and riders. 🌱 Learn fast in an entrepreneurial environment Work close to the market with autonomy, pace and real responsibility. 🧠 Build a career, not just a role Stretch yourself, develop new skills and grow as the business evolves. 🌎 Deliver together in an inclusive culture Collaborative, values-driven teams that support how you work best. We aim to create a fair process that lets your skills shine—our interview typically includes 3-4 stages. Find more about how we hire here. Our Global Structure Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team. Diversity, Equity and Inclusion At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong. We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief. If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience. If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you! Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-deliveroo ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-field-based-business-development-executive-newcastle-329418" ;
    schema:jobLocation [ a schema:Place ;
            schema:name "Newcastle" ] ;
    schema:title "Field-Based Business Development Executive - Newcastle" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/deliveroo/field-based-business-development-executive-newcastle-329418> .

