    schema:description "**This position is based in Germany with hybrid or remote working options. Applicants must hold a valid work/residence permit for the respective location.** Chaos is a leading global software company that provides world-class visualization and design solutions, empowering creative minds to bring ideas to life. For over twenty years, Chaos has developed innovative technologies serving multiple industries, including architecture and design, media and entertainment, and product e-commerce. Chaos’ solutions help architects, designers, VFX artists/animators, and other creative professionals share ideas, optimize workflows, and create immersive experiences. Headquartered in Karlsruhe, Germany, Chaos is a global company with offices in 11 cities worldwide. In 2022, Chaos and Enscape merged, bringing together two industry-leading companies into one. Since then, Chaos has continued to grow with the additions of Cylindo, AXYZ Design, and Evolve Lab, further expanding our expertise and solutions across architecture, design, e-commerce, and AI. For more information, please visit chaos.com. Role Overview The Working Student supports the GTM Strategy & Transformation function, working directly with the Senior Director on high-impact strategic and operational priorities. The role contributes to market research, competitive analysis, process improvement, and growth initiatives that directly support the revenue organisation's go-to-market execution. This is a hands-on, project-based role suited to a student with strong analytical foundations, an interest in commercial strategy, and the initiative to take ownership of outcomes rather than just tasks. Main Responsibilities Support the end-to-end delivery of high-priority GTM initiatives: tracking milestones, managing stakeholder inputs, and ensuring projects deliver measurable outcomes. Identify bottlenecks and inefficiencies in go-to-market processes, proposing and helping implement frameworks that improve scalability across the organisation. Translate data and analysis into structured, concise storylines and presentations for senior stakeholders. Conduct market research and competitive benchmarking, synthesising findings into clear briefings and recommendations that support executive-level decision-making. Work closely with the Senior Director, GTM Strategy & Transformation and cross-functional teams to support evolving strategic priorities as they arise. Required Experience Currently pursuing a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Business, Engineering, Marketing, or a related field. Previous experience in a fast-paced environment, such as a startup, venture-backed company, or management consultancy, is a strong advantage. Required Skills Analytical and structured: goes beyond surface-level data, questions assumptions, and draws independent, well-reasoned conclusions. Takes initiative and ownership: identifies problems, proposes solutions, and follows through to implementation without waiting to be directed. Comfortable operating in ambiguous environments where projects don't have an established playbook. Able to structure complex ideas in writing and produce concise, high-quality output for senior audiences. Collaborative and adaptable: works effectively across functions and adjusts quickly to shifting priorities. Fluent in English. Please note: This is a working student position, limited to a maximum of 20 hours per week during the semester. Applicants must be currently enrolled at a university and provide valid proof of enrollment (“Immatrikulationsbescheinigung” in Germany). Compensation is hourly €18. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Entry, parttime minijob" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-chaos ;
